    "updated_at": "2026-11-17T00:08:57Z",
    "body": "Thank you for this clear request, and for the offer to test on a LinuxCNC 2.9 sim and on your machine. That helps a lot.\n\nTriage: `P6` (an accepted enhancement), `effort:high` (it changes posted G-code, so it gets the full safety review). Your option list is a good scope for a first `linuxcnc.cps` and a `linuxcnc-3axis.mch`: retract choice, tool change with or without `G43`, `G64 P` or `G61`, the safe start block, canned cycles with the rigid-tap refusal, and incremental IJK arcs.\n\nTo help, please add these if you can:\n1. The axis section of your `.ini` (travel limits, and where machine Z0 is: top or bottom of travel).\n2. What your `M6` remap does: does it apply the tool length itself, and where does it move before the change?\n3. Later, one posted program run through the LinuxCNC sim, and then a safe air cut.\n\nClean-room note: please send only your own configuration and programs. Do not send output from Fusion 360 or HSMWorks, or posts from other CAM programs.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
