    "updated_at": "2026-11-17T22:21:50Z",
    "body": "Thanks for picking this up so quickly. Here are the answers to your questions, taken from my machine's config (LinuxCNC 2.9, Remora):\n\n**1. Axis limits and home**\n\n```\n[AXIS_X] MIN_LIMIT = -0.01   MAX_LIMIT = 380.0\n[AXIS_Y] MIN_LIMIT = -540.0  MAX_LIMIT = 0.01\n[AXIS_Z] MIN_LIMIT = -115    MAX_LIMIT = 0.1\n[JOINT_2] HOME = 0   HOME_OFFSET = 5.0   (switch at the top)\n```\n\n**Machine Z0 is the top of travel**, so `G53 G0 Z0` is my safe retract. My tool-change macros already retract there. For my machine file: `safe_retract: 0`.\n\n**2. The M6 remap**\n\n`REMAP=M6 modalgroup=6 prolog=change_prolog ngc=<my sub> epilog=change_epilog` (stdglue). It runs `G49` first, retracts to `G53 Z0`, then changes the tool (from an automatic changer pocket, or as a manual change). It then measures the new tool on a tool setter, writes the result with `G10 L1 P<tool> Z...` and **applies `G43` itself**.\n\nSo a posted `G43 H<n>` after `M6` does no harm on my machine: it selects the entry that was just measured. Please keep it **on by default**, though. Tool measurement can be switched off in the GUI, and the remap then returns with `G49` still active and no `G43`. In that case the posted `G43 H<n>` is the only thing that applies a length offset.\n\n**3. Spindle encoder:** none. Nothing drives `spindle.0.revs` in my HAL, so `rigid_tapping` stays false, and refusing taps is the right behaviour for me.\n\n**4. An early interpreter check of the goldens**\n\nI ran the 13 LinuxCNC goldens at `95b83ca` (the 12 files in `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/` plus `synth_linuxcnc.nc`) through the LinuxCNC 2.9 interpreter: standalone `rs274` with `-T`, tools 1–4 in a tool table, no `M6` remap.\n\n- All 13 run to `PROGRAM_END` with no errors or warnings.\n- All 103 arcs (`G91.1` incremental IJK) are accepted, and so are `G73`, `G81`, `G82` and `G83`.\n- Every feed move has the spindle running and a tool length offset in effect.\n- The `G53 G0 Z0` retracts land at machine Z0 with the offset active, which is what I want.\n\nOnce the PR is in a release, I'll post a real program for my machine and report the sim run and an air cut, as offered.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
